gitleaks
================================================================================

`src/core/rules/secrets.toml` contains secret-detection patterns and
false-positive test cases derived from gitleaks:

    https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks

    version v8.30.1
    commit  83d9cd684c87d95d656c1458ef04895a7f1cbd8e

That commit is pinned in `scripts/secret-rules/build.py` and its config file is
checksummed there, so the derivation is reproducible and this attribution names
a specific revision rather than a moving branch.

The patterns were curated and, in two documented cases, narrowed for scanning
command output rather than repository contents. Some were also rewritten for
the `regex` crate's syntax (explicit ASCII classes, escaped literal braces);
those rewrites are behaviour-preserving on ASCII input and are described in
`src/core/rules/README.md`. Each rule records its upstream rule id in its `id`
field. Regeneration tooling lives in `scripts/secret-rules/`.

